# Fal-X scope allowlist.
#
# Everything here is reachable, and nothing else is. The file is required and it
# fails closed: an absent, empty or unreadable allowlist refuses the run rather
# than defaulting to anything.
#
# Copy this file to config/scope.txt and replace the examples. The two entries
# below are placeholders that match nothing real.
#
# Syntax, one entry per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

#   example.com              the domain and every subdomain
#   *.wild.test              subdomains only, not wild.test itself
#   192.0.2.0/24             an address range (RFC 5737 documentation space)
#   2001:db8::1              an address (RFC 3849 documentation space)
#   example.com:8443         one port on one host
#
# A bare * is refused unless you pass --allow-any, and it asks for confirmation
# before proceeding.
#
# Subdomain matching is label-aware. example.com matches example.com and
# api.example.com. It does not match example.com.attacker.test, notexample.com,
# or evil-example.com.
#
# Private, loopback, link-local, carrier-NAT and cloud-metadata ranges are denied
# even when listed here, unless you pass --allow-private.

example.com
*.wild.test
192.0.2.0/24